caption: Importer pack fields
tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/reference
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/reference/pack-fields
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

An //importer pack// is a plugin that carries one profile and a panel
tiddler.  The panel tiddler's fields configure the runtime's consumer
panel (`$:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert/ui/consumer-panel`), which the
panel tiddler transcludes with `pack=` set to its own title.  The demo
wiki ships one, `$:/plugins/crosseye/reading-list-importer`, hand-built
as the reference for what the [[generator|$:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/generator]] emits.

|!Field           |!Required |!Purpose                                                  |
|`slug`           |yes       |Namespace key; working data lives under `$:/temp/json-convert/<slug>/` |
|`profile`        |yes       |Title of the profile tiddler (inside the pack)            |
|`caption`        |yes       |Tab caption, e.g. //Import Invoices//                     |
|`tags`           |yes       |`$:/tags/SideBar` puts the panel in the sidebar           |
|`description`    |no        |Wikitext shown at the top of the panel                    |
|`sample`         |no        |Title of a JSON tiddler offered by ''Try it with the sample'' |
|`convert-label`  |no        |Label for the Convert button (default ''Convert'')        |
|`apply-label`    |no        |Label for the Apply button (default ''Apply'')            |
|`collisions`     |no        |Default decision for existing titles: `skip` (default) or `overwrite` |
|`runtime-min`    |no        |Lowest runtime version the pack needs; the panel warns below it |
|`studio-url`     |no        |Where the pack was made; every "ask whoever made this" message links here |

Alongside the panel tiddler the pack holds `<pack>/profile`, optional
`<pack>/sample` and `<pack>/shape` (the sample's record shape, as
`engine/shape.js` merges it, with the records path and count), and one
`<pack>/transforms/<name>` per custom transform the profile references.
The plugin tiddler itself carries `json-convert-pack: <slug>` so the
studio can list the packs it has made.

The profile carries `"format": 1` so a future runtime that no longer
reads that format can say so.  The panel tiddler's text is a small shim:
if the runtime's consumer panel exists it transcludes it, otherwise it
shows a sentence saying which plugin to install and where to get it.
